.TH XDG-DESKTOP-PORTAL-FL 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
xdg-desktop-portal-fl \- fldesktop backend for xdg-desktop-portal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBxdg-desktop-portal-fl\fR [\fB\-\-replace\fR]
.br
\fBxdg-desktop-portal-fl \-\-activate\-shortcut\fR \fIAPP_ID\fR \fISHORTCUT_ID\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Implements the desktop side of the XDG desktop portals for fldesktop
sessions, so that sandboxed (Flatpak, Snap) and portal aware programs get
fldesktop dialogs and settings:
.TP
\fBFileChooser\fR
open, save and "save several files" dialogs with places, bookmarks
(\fI~/.config/gtk-3.0/bookmarks\fR), filters and choices.
.TP
\fBAppChooser\fR
the "open with" dialog.
.TP
\fBSettings\fR
the color scheme, accent color, icon theme and fonts of
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/desktop.ini\fR; changes are announced right away.
.TP
\fBScreenshot\fR
screenshots with \fBgrim\fR(1) (areas and color picking with \fBslurp\fR(1)),
saved in the Screenshots folder of the Pictures directory.
.TP
\fBAccess\fR, \fBAccount\fR
permission and "share your details" dialogs.
.TP
\fBNotification\fR
passes notifications on to \fBfl-notifyd\fR(1).
.TP
\fBWallpaper\fR
sets the desktop background.
.TP
\fBScreenCast\fR
screen sharing for browsers, video calls and recorders: a dialog picks a
screen or a single window, which is then sent as a PipeWire video stream.
Applications may ask to remember the choice. Windows can be shared when
\fBfl-wm\fR(1) is built with wlroots 0.20 or newer; with wlroots 0.18 only
whole screens can be shared (through wlr-screencopy).
.TP
\fBRemoteDesktop\fR
remote control: after asking, the application moves the pointer, clicks,
scrolls and types (through a virtual pointer and keyboard with the session's
keyboard layout), usually together with screen sharing. Touch input is not
offered.
.TP
\fBInhibit\fR
keeps the screen on (an idle inhibitor \fBfl-wm\fR(1) honours) and the computer
from suspending (a logind inhibitor lock) while an application asks.
.TP
\fBBackground\fR
running in the background is allowed; starting with the session writes
\fI~/.config/autostart/APP_ID.desktop\fR, which \fBfl-autostart\fR(1) starts.
.TP
\fBGlobalShortcuts\fR
asks once which keys to use for the shortcuts an application wants and stores
them in \fI~/.config/fldesktop/global-shortcuts.ini\fR; \fBfl-wm\fR(1) binds
them (never over a binding of its own) and runs
\fBxdg-desktop-portal-fl \-\-activate\-shortcut\fR when one is pressed. Settings >
Shortcuts > Application Shortcuts lists and removes them.
.TP
\fBPrint\fR
a print dialog (printer, copies, pages, sides) and printing through CUPS.
.PP
Other portals are left to the GTK backend (and xdg-desktop-portal-wlr is
the fallback for screen casting), as listed in
\fI/usr/share/xdg-desktop-portal/fldesktop-portals.conf\fR. The program is
started by D-Bus; \fBfl-autostart\fR(1) passes WAYLAND_DISPLAY to D-Bus
activated programs at login.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-replace\fR
Take over from a running instance.
.TP
\fB\-\-activate\-shortcut\fR \fIAPP_ID\fR \fISHORTCUT_ID\fR
Tell the running portal that a global shortcut was pressed (\fBfl-wm\fR(1) does).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-notifyd\fR(1), \fBflatpak\fR(1), \fBgrim\fR(1), \fBslurp\fR(1)
